{"book":19,"chapter":18,"rubric":"STORAGE / CHAPTER 18","slides":[{"title":"Why a SAN","sub":"Chapter 18 · Storage","short":"SAN","main":"A shared array gives hosts devices (LUNs), recognized by WWID.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Array","LUN","Initiator","oVirt"],"captions":["VM disks live not on host drives but on a shared array","The array hands out block devices, LUNs; the array side is the target","The server that uses them is the initiator; a disk is known by WWID, not by sdb","An oVirt block domain is an LVM volume group on such LUNs"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"shared disk array (target)","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"shared disk array (target)","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"LUN: block device with a WWID","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"shared disk array (target)","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"LUN: block device with a WWID","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"host (initiator) over iSCSI or FC","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"shared disk array (target)","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"LUN: block device with a WWID","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"host (initiator) over iSCSI or FC","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n3","x":180.0,"y":122.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"oVirt: domain = VG on LUNs","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[7.8,17.8,29.2]}]},{"title":"iSCSI names and portals","sub":"Chapter 18 · Storage","short":"IQN","main":"An IQN names initiator and target; a portal is an address with port 3260.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Initiator","Target","Portals","Session"],"captions":["The host name is in initiatorname.iscsi, unique per host","The target has an IQN too: iqn, year-month, reversed domain, a string after a colon","Portals lead to the target: address, port 3260 and a portal group tag","A login creates an initiator-portal session managed by iscsid"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["# /etc/iscsi/initiatorname.iscsi","InitiatorName=iqn.1994-05.com.redhat:7a9c1f","","# target and its two portals","iqn.2003-01.org.linux-iscsi.san1:sn.a1","  10.0.0.1:3260,1","  10.0.1.1:3260,2"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["# /etc/iscsi/initiatorname.iscsi","InitiatorName=iqn.1994-05.com.redhat:7a9c1f","","# target and its two portals","iqn.2003-01.org.linux-iscsi.san1:sn.a1","  10.0.0.1:3260,1","  10.0.1.1:3260,2"],"hl":[4],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["# /etc/iscsi/initiatorname.iscsi","InitiatorName=iqn.1994-05.com.redhat:7a9c1f","","# target and its two portals","iqn.2003-01.org.linux-iscsi.san1:sn.a1","  10.0.0.1:3260,1","  10.0.1.1:3260,2"],"hl":[5,6],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["# /etc/iscsi/initiatorname.iscsi","InitiatorName=iqn.1994-05.com.redhat:7a9c1f","","# target and its two portals","iqn.2003-01.org.linux-iscsi.san1:sn.a1","  10.0.0.1:3260,1","  10.0.1.1:3260,2"],"hl":[5,6],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[7.4,18.3,27.4]}]},{"title":"Three steps to connect","sub":"Chapter 18 · Storage","short":"iscsiadm","main":"Discovery writes records, login creates a session, startup makes it permanent.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Discovery","Login","Startup","CHAP"],"captions":["Discovery asks the portal for targets and writes records under /var/lib/iscsi","Login to a record creates a session, new disks appear","node.startup automatic repeats the login at boot; the default is manual","A password is set in iscsid.conf or the record: authmethod CHAP, username, password"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["iscsiadm -m discovery -t st -p 10.0.0.1","10.0.0.1:3260,1 iqn.2003-01.org.x:sn.a1","","iscsiadm -m node -T iqn.2003-01.org.x:sn.a1 \\","  -p 10.0.0.1 -l","iscsiadm -m node -T iqn.2003-01.org.x:sn.a1 \\","  -p 10.0.0.1 --op update -n node.startup \\","  -v automatic"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["iscsiadm -m discovery -t st -p 10.0.0.1","10.0.0.1:3260,1 iqn.2003-01.org.x:sn.a1","","iscsiadm -m node -T iqn.2003-01.org.x:sn.a1 \\","  -p 10.0.0.1 -l","iscsiadm -m node -T iqn.2003-01.org.x:sn.a1 \\","  -p 10.0.0.1 --op update -n node.startup \\","  -v automatic"],"hl":[3,4],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["iscsiadm -m discovery -t st -p 10.0.0.1","10.0.0.1:3260,1 iqn.2003-01.org.x:sn.a1","","iscsiadm -m node -T iqn.2003-01.org.x:sn.a1 \\","  -p 10.0.0.1 -l","iscsiadm -m node -T iqn.2003-01.org.x:sn.a1 \\","  -p 10.0.0.1 --op update -n node.startup \\","  -v automatic"],"hl":[5,6,7],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["iscsiadm -m discovery -t st -p 10.0.0.1","10.0.0.1:3260,1 iqn.2003-01.org.x:sn.a1","","iscsiadm -m node -T iqn.2003-01.org.x:sn.a1 \\","  -p 10.0.0.1 -l","iscsiadm -m node -T iqn.2003-01.org.x:sn.a1 \\","  -p 10.0.0.1 --op update -n node.startup \\","  -v automatic"],"hl":[5,6,7],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[11.1,18.7,28.9]}]},{"title":"Session state","sub":"Chapter 18 · Storage","short":"Sessions","main":"The session list, the -P tree and the 120-second replacement timeout.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["List","Target","State","Disks"],"captions":["iscsiadm -m session: transport, session id, portal with tag, target name","-P 1 groups by target and shows the portal","A healthy session: Connection State LOGGED IN, Session State LOGGED_IN","-P 3 adds the disks behind it; on a drop the kernel waits replacement_timeout, 120 s"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["tcp: [1] 10.0.0.1:3260,1 iqn.2003-01.org.x:sn.a1 (non-flash)","Target: iqn.2003-01.org.x:sn.a1 (non-flash)","  Current Portal: 10.0.0.1:3260,1","    iSCSI Connection State: LOGGED IN","    iSCSI Session State: LOGGED_IN","    Attached scsi disk sdb   State: running"],"hl":[0],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["tcp: [1] 10.0.0.1:3260,1 iqn.2003-01.org.x:sn.a1 (non-flash)","Target: iqn.2003-01.org.x:sn.a1 (non-flash)","  Current Portal: 10.0.0.1:3260,1","    iSCSI Connection State: LOGGED IN","    iSCSI Session State: LOGGED_IN","    Attached scsi disk sdb   State: running"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["tcp: [1] 10.0.0.1:3260,1 iqn.2003-01.org.x:sn.a1 (non-flash)","Target: iqn.2003-01.org.x:sn.a1 (non-flash)","  Current Portal: 10.0.0.1:3260,1","    iSCSI Connection State: LOGGED IN","    iSCSI Session State: LOGGED_IN","    Attached scsi disk sdb   State: running"],"hl":[3,4],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["tcp: [1] 10.0.0.1:3260,1 iqn.2003-01.org.x:sn.a1 (non-flash)","Target: iqn.2003-01.org.x:sn.a1 (non-flash)","  Current Portal: 10.0.0.1:3260,1","    iSCSI Connection State: LOGGED IN","    iSCSI Session State: LOGGED_IN","    Attached scsi disk sdb   State: running"],"hl":[5],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[10.7,17.0,27.5]}]},{"title":"Fibre Channel","sub":"Chapter 18 · Storage","short":"FC","main":"HBA, WWPN, zoning on the fabric and masking on the array.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["HBA","WWPN","Zones","Timers"],"captions":["The host has an HBA; the adapter and its ports have worldwide names","The WWPN is a port address, like a MAC on Ethernet; ports are in /sys/class/fc_host","Zoning on the switches decides who sees whom; masking on the array picks LUNs","dev_loss_tmo keeps a lost port, fast_io_fail_tmo returns errors sooner"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":95.0,"y":50.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"HBA adapter\nin the host","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":95.0,"y":50.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"HBA adapter\nin the host","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":265.0,"y":50.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"WWPN: port\naddress","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":95.0,"y":50.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"HBA adapter\nin the host","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":265.0,"y":50.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"WWPN: port\naddress","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":95.0,"y":110.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"zoning and\nmasking","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":95.0,"y":50.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"HBA adapter\nin the host","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":265.0,"y":50.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"WWPN: port\naddress","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":95.0,"y":110.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"zoning and\nmasking","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n3","x":265.0,"y":110.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"timers\ndev_loss, fast_io","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[8.4,18.8,28.4]}]},{"title":"One LUN, two disks","sub":"Chapter 18 · Storage","short":"Path","main":"Two paths give sdb and sdc; multipathd joins them by WWID into one map.","body":[{"t":"s